# p_2f7a — Saturday Around the House: Guitar Afternoon, Puzzle Morning, Relaxed Kitchen

The Saturday message — "It's the weekend, so we're off our usual routine and around the house more" — tells us both residents are home all day with no fixed work schedule. Hana does not commute, so her laptop, keys, jacket, handbag, wallet, and pen are in the house. Priya takes her late-morning walk (roughly 10–11) and Hana may slip out for errands around midday (12–15), but the dominant pattern is two people orbiting the kitchen and living room.

What sets this document apart: it predicts a *structured leisure* Saturday. Hana plays guitar in the mid-afternoon (15–17), pulling it off the bedroom floor. Priya works on her jigsaw puzzle in the late morning (11–14), pulling the box from the bookshelf to the coffee table. Evening is a shared movie on the couch (20–22), with the remote migrating from the TV stand to the couch. The kitchen sees a relaxed brunch (11–12) and a lighter dinner (18–19), so the pot and pan sit in the cupboard for most of the day.

This document is refuted if: the guitar is never seen off the bedroom floor on a Saturday; the puzzle box never reaches the coffee table; Hana's commute objects are found at entry locations only during hours that conflict with an errand window; or the residents are seen in the kitchen at 21:00+ (suggesting a late dinner rather than the 18:00 one).

