# p_5d8b — Weekend Kitchen: Brunch at Eleven, Light Dinner at Six

The Saturday message says the household is "off its usual routine." The weekday kitchen rhythm (pot and pan in the cupboard until 17:30, then a single dinner cooking window at 18–20) breaks down on weekends. Instead there are two shorter cooking windows: a relaxed brunch around 11–12 and a lighter dinner around 18–19. Between those windows the pot and pan go back to the cupboard. The recipe book stays on the counter all weekend (less structured cooking, easier reference). The cutting board and knife are pulled to the counter only during the two cooking windows.

This document is distinguished from p_4c8f (weekday dinner at 19) by shifting the cooking windows earlier and adding a brunch. It is distinguished from p_7d4a (late evening kitchen, dinner at 20) by putting dinner at 18 and adding the 11 o'clock brunch. It is distinguished from p_c1d6 (split cooking, two windows on weekdays) by making both windows weekend-only and attributing them to shared cooking rather than one person per meal.

Refuted if: the pot is on the counter at 14:00 on a Saturday (no midday cooking); the pan is in the cupboard at 11:30 on a Saturday (no brunch); the recipe book is in the pantry rather than on the counter during a weekend cooking window; or the kitchen table has no plates at 11:30 on a Saturday.

